Knowledge slices — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
============================================================================

Everything under `kb/` — the curated slice guides (`README.md`), the findings
(`findings.yaml`) and the evidence files — is licensed under CC BY 4.0:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt the facts, including commercially, as long as you give
appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate whether you changed
anything. A finding you reuse is credited by its `id` and `author` fields.

The rest of the repository (`tools/`, `recipes/`, `firmware/`, `agents/`,
`proposals/`, CI) is MIT — see `../LICENSE`.

Why the split: code rots and gets rewritten, so it wants the most permissive
licence there is. Facts are the durable part and they want attribution, because
attribution is what lets the next person judge how far to trust a fact and where
to go to argue with it.

Findings are *observations about hardware we do not own and did not design*.
They are recorded for interoperability and repair. Reverse engineering for
interoperability is lawful in the EU (Directive 2009/24/EC art. 6); the facts
in this repository were obtained that way. No vendor firmware, no vendor ROM
dump and no derivative of either is distributed here — see `../CONTRIBUTING.md`
for the deny-list that keeps it that way.
